OL,3,AWinter energy prices expected to rise
OL,4,Ato three-year high
OL,5,
OL,6,FEnergy bills for millions of households
OL,7,Fare expected to rise this winter to the
OL,8,Fhighest level for three years, under a
OL,9,Fprice cap to be announced by the
OL,10,Findustry regulator on Wednesday.
OL,12,FThe cap will reflect the rise in the
OL,13,Fwholesale cost of gas, paid by
OL,14,Fsuppliers and will hit bills just as
OL,15,Fthe colder weather arrives in October
OL,16,Funtil the end of December.
OL,18,FAnalysts expect Ofgem to say prices
OL,19,Fwill go up by 4% compared with the
OL,20,Fcurrent cap, affecting those on
OL,21,Fvariable tariffs in England, Scotland
OL,22,Fand Wales.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
